{"case_id":"C032","gap_exists":true,"gap_type":["API protocol","stateful suspension/resumption","harness compatibility"],"confidence":99,"affected_functions":["fuzz/c/std/gif_fuzzer.c:fuzz","fuzz/c/std/zlib_fuzzer.c:fuzz","wuffs_deflate__decoder__decode","wuffs_gif__decoder__decode_image_config","wuffs_gif__decoder__decode_frame_config","wuffs_gif__decoder__decode_frame","WUFFS_BASE__COROUTINE_SUSPENSION_POINT_MAYBE_SUSPEND"],"reason":"S1 changes wuffs_base__status from a struct with .code to a const char* whose NULL, '$'-prefixed, and other values mean OK, suspension, and error. Both H0 fuzz functions still access z.code, so they are incompatible with S1. Even after mechanical conversion, H0 supplies one fixed src_reader and terminates on SHORT_READ instead of replenishing input and resuming the same decoder. It therefore misses the stateful short-read coroutine protocol directly affected by the new pointer-based status classification and suspension macro.","evidence":["S1 declares `typedef const char* wuffs_base__status` and implements `wuffs_base__status__is_suspension` as `z && (*z == '$')`.","Both H0 functions repeatedly use `z.code`; gif_fuzzer.c also compares it with `WUFFS_BASE__SUSPENSION_END_OF_DATA`, while zlib_fuzzer.c compares it with `WUFFS_BASE__SUSPENSION_SHORT_WRITE`.","zlib_fuzzer.c resumes `wuffs_zlib__decoder__decode` only after `WUFFS_BASE__SUSPENSION_SHORT_WRITE`; any other status, including short read, breaks the loop.","gif_fuzzer.c exits on every non-OK result from `wuffs_gif__decoder__decode_image_config` or `wuffs_gif__decoder__decode_frame`; it never resumes after `wuffs_base__suspension__short_read`.","The S1 diff changes many `wuffs_deflate__decoder__decode_*` and `wuffs_gif__decoder__decode_*` coroutine paths to return `wuffs_base__suspension__short_read`, and changes `WUFFS_BASE__COROUTINE_SUSPENSION_POINT_MAYBE_SUSPEND` to classify status strings by their first character."],"recommended_action":"Update H0 to use the S1 status API (`z`, `wuffs_base__status__is_*`, and pointer status symbols), then add fuzz-controlled source chunking that repeatedly appends/reveals bytes and resumes the same GIF or zlib decoder after `wuffs_base__suspension__short_read`; retain the existing zlib short-write progress check and exercise combinations of short reads and short writes."}
